# Lua

# Instances
An instance can be anything. Script, part, model, etc.

# Scripts
In luau there are multiple kinds of files.
Scripts, moduleScripts and localScripts.

Scripts and localScripts are executed at start.
moduleScripts require one of the others to call them.
To do that the require function is called.
This function will return what is returned in the called file.

Scripts run on server side and local side.
Local Scripts are used for user-specific services.
The Server Scripts handle everything else.

# Instantiation, Initialisation, Construction
Instantiation is the process of creation of the component.
Initialisation is the starting of it's logic.
Construction encompases both. (I made it up)

# Events
An event makes several scripts able to communicate in real time through signals.
:Fire(...) will send a signal.
.Event:Connect(function) will catch a fired signal.

## Subscribe, Publish, Topic
A topic is a channel categorising messages.
A pubblisher broadcasts a message with a specific topic.
A Subscriber catches and reacts to the messages from the topic he's listening for.

## BindableEvent
A Bindable event is limited to same-side scripts. (only local or only on the server)

# Services
Services are global singleton objects provided by Roblox.
Accessed via "game:GetService(ServiceName)".

## Players (service)
Manages Players instances in game
The event starting when a player joins is ".PlayerAdded"
To get all players: ":GetPlayers()"

## DataStoreService
Provides persistent storage across sessions.
To create and get a data store: ":GetDataStore(name)"
To write to it: ".SetAsync(key, data)"
To read from it: ".GetAsync(key)"

# Attributes
Attributes are variables stored in an instance.
Accessed via: "instance:GetAttribute(AttributeName)"

# Parts
Parts are 3D physical objects.

# Players
Players are the object containing an individual's data

## Characters
Player's 3D models.

# Models
A model is a group of instances.

# CFrames
Cframes are a data structure containing the model's coordinates and angle in 3D.

# Templates
Pre-made objects stored and cloned at runtime to create new instances.

# Cloning
Duplicating any instance can be done using "instance:Clone(void)"

# Tables
Lua uses extensively tables as the most basic data structure.
an empty table is defined as "{}".

## Metatables
A metatable is what defines custom behaviors for a table.
__index makes a table search for a key it doesn't have.
This makes tables able to access methods from other tables.
Alike inheritance.
To set a metatable use "setmetatable(destination, origin)".
It returns the metatable we assign it to.

# Folders
We can search an instance in a folder using "folder[key]".
The key being the name of the instance we're looking for.

# Leaderboard
The leaderboard is a UI showing any state we want.

# Threads
Threads are executions of code running in parallel to the main program.
The table used for threads is "coroutine".
".create" makes a new thread.
".wrap(function)" makes a new thread for the given function.

# For loops
For loops can iterate over a table, taking a table's value at each step.
To get the index and the value we can use "for key, value in ipairs(table)".
To ignore one replace it by "_".


# Code structure
A Tycoon is the entire structure that a player plays in.
It is composed itself of different "modules", that we can call "parts"

